# Closed-class words that never stand as a counted noun right after an hour:
# pronouns, adverbs and verb particles ("a las 8 te llamo").  Each word's class
# is quoted from its Wiktionary entry (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the
# fetched pages are kept with the audit.  Markup is removed from the quotes.
# me: Pronoun. "me direct object"
# te: Pronoun. "(direct object) you"
# le: Pronoun. "(direct object) him, her, it, them"
# la: Pronoun. "her, it (direct object)"
# lui: Pronoun. "him, he, it; the third-person masculine singular personal pronoun used after a preposition, or as the predi..."
# nous: Pronoun. "the plural personal pronoun in the first person"
# vous: Pronoun. "the plural personal pronoun in the second person"
# leur: Pronoun. "(personal, indirect) (to) them"
# y: Pronoun. "there (at a place)"
# en: Pronoun. "Used as the object of a verb to indicate an indefinite quantity; of it, of them. Replaces the partitive art..."
me
te
le
la
lui
nous
vous
leur
y
en
